  "summary": "The identified studies apply transformer-based architectures, specifically self-attention encoder models, to the domain of battery health, focusing on the task of estimating battery remaining life [V0077, V0080, V0079, V0078]. These methods are evaluated across several datasets, including CellLife, ProtMap, GridWatch, and ToxiBench [V0077, V0080, V0079, V0078]. Reported performance metrics vary, with AUROC values reaching 0.87 on CellLife and F1 scores reaching 0.94 on ToxiBench [V0077, V0078]. Additionally, a study on estimating battery remaining life utilized decentralised training, achieving an AUROC of 0.84 on ProtMap [V0084].",
